        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0118" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg58"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Dr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Aug, 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 385.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 338, of January 31,
                    1895, in regard to the killing of American seamen at Santa Catharina, I have the
                    honor to inclose copy and translation of a note from this Government showing the
                    efforts made by the authorities for the punishment of the guilty.</p>
                <p>Of the four soldiers originally charged with the crime one has been acquitted and
                    another is dead, thus leaving only two, who it appears were convicted in the
                    lower court but have taken an appeal, the result of which is yet unknown. The
                    authorities are apparently using all diligence to secure a conviction, and I
                    have no doubt but what the result will be satisfactory.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. L.
                    Thompson</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d49-a1.xml" xpointer="d49-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
